       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it might be a typo.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg PO daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.** Labeled dosing for adults is usually 50\u2013200 mg/day, and 200 mg/day is the ceiling for all indications. A single 1000 mg dose is in overdose territory, with risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures and QTc prolongation.\n\nThe most likely intended order is one of these:\n- **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily**, if a zero was added by mistake\n- **Sertraline 50 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose\n- **Sertraline 200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose\n\nWhich dose did you mean? Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is intended for a specific reason, please tell me the reason. I'd still recommend a pharmacy review before an order that far above the maximum goes through."
